G514.b:
⟪ἄξιος⟫, -α, -ον
(< ἄγω, in sense, to weigh), [in LXX for ⁨בֵּן⁩ (⟦Deuteronomy 25:2|De 25:2⟧), ⁨מָלֵא⁩, ⁨שָׁוָה⁩; freq. in Wis, II Mac;]
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪of weight⟫, ⟪worth⟫ (often c. gen., cf. ⟦Proverbs 3:15|Pr 3:15⟧ ⟦Proverbs 8:11|8:11⟧), seq. πρός: ⟦Romans 8:18|Ro 8:18⟧ (v. Field, Notes, 157);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪befitting⟫, ⟪meet⟫: c. gen., ⟦Matthew 3:8|Mt 3:8⟧, ⟦Luke 3:8|Lk 3:8⟧ ⟦Luke 23:41|23:41⟧, ⟦Acts 26:20|Ac 26:20⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:4|I Co 16:4⟧ (v. M, Pr., 216); absol., ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:3|II Th 1:3⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of persons, ⟪worthy⟫;
	⟪α⟫ in good sense: c. gen. rei, ⟦Matthew 10:10|Mt 10:10⟧, ⟦Luke 7:4|Lk 7:4⟧ ⟦Luke 10:7|10:7⟧, ⟦Acts 13:46|Ac 13:46⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 1:15|I Ti 1:15⟧ ⟦1 Timothy 4:9|4:9⟧ ⟦1 Timothy 5:18|5:18⟧ ⟦1 Timothy 6:1|6:1⟧; c. aor. inf. (v. M, Pr., 203): ⟦Luke 15:19|Lk 15:19⟧, ⟦Luke 15:21|21⟧, ⟦Acts 13:25|Ac 13:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:11|Re 4:11⟧ ⟦Revelation 5:2|5:2⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:4|4⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:9|9⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:12|12⟧; seq. ἵνα: ⟦John 1:27|Jo 1:27⟧; ὅς, ⟦Luke 7:4|Lk 7:4⟧; absol., but of what understood: ⟦Matthew 10:11|Mt 10:11⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:13|13⟧ ⟦Matthew 22:8|22:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:4|Re 3:4⟧; c. gen. pers., ⟦Matthew 10:37|Mt 10:37⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:38|38⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:38|He 11:38⟧;
	⟪β⟫ in bad sense; c. gen. rei, ⟦Luke 12:48|Lk 12:48⟧ ⟦Luke 23:15|23:15⟧, ⟦Acts 23:29|Ac 23:29⟧ ⟦Acts 25:11|25:11⟧, ⟦Acts 25:25|25⟧ ⟦Acts 26:31|26:31⟧, ⟦Romans 1:32|Ro 1:32⟧; absol., ⟦Revelation 16:6|Re 16:6⟧ (MM, VGT, s.v.).†

G565.b:
⟪ἀπ-έρχομαι⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨הלךְ⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to go away⟫, ⟪depart⟫ (also, in late writers, with "perfective" force, ⟪to arrive⟫ at a destination, the thought being carried on to the goal; M, Pr., 111 f., 247; MM, s.v.);
	⟪(a)⟫ absol.: ⟦Matthew 13:25|Mt 13:25⟧, al.; ptcp., ἀπελθών, used pleonastically with other verbs as in Heb. (Dalman, Words, 21), ⟦Matthew 13:28|Mt 13:28⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ with mention of place or person: εἰς, ⟦Matthew 14:15|Mt 14:15⟧; ἐπί, ⟦Luke 24:24|Lk 24:24⟧; πρός, ⟦Revelation 10:9|Re 10:9⟧; ἀπό, ⟦Luke 1:38|Lk 1:38⟧; ἐξω, ⟦Acts 4:15|Ac 4:15⟧; ἐκεῖ, ⟦Matthew 2:22|Mt 2:22⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As in LXX, seq. ὀπίσω, c. gen. (Heb. ⁨הָלַךְ אַחֲרֵי⁩), ⟪to go after⟫, ⟪follow⟫: ⟦Mark 1:20|Mk 1:20⟧, ⟦John 12:19|Jo 12:19⟧; metaph., ⟦Mark 1:42|Mk 1:42⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:1|Re 21:1⟧.

G575.b:
⟪ἀπό⟫ (on the freq. neglect of elision bef. vowels, v. Tdf., Pr., 94, WH, App., 146), prep. c. gen. (WM, 462 ff.; on its relation to ἐκ, παρά, ὑπό, WM, 456 f.),
[in LXX for ⁨מִן⁩, ⁨בְּ⁩, ⁨לְ⁩;] ⟪from⟫ (i.e. from the exterior).
⟪1.⟫ Of separation and cessation;
	⟪(1)⟫ of motion from a place: ⟦Matthew 5:29|Mt 5:29⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:30|30⟧ ⟦Matthew 7:23|7:23⟧, ⟦Luke 5:2|Lk 5:2⟧ ⟦Luke 22:41|22:41⟧, al.;
	⟪(2)⟫ in partitive sense (M, Pr., 72, 102, 245; MM, s.v.; Bl., § 40, 2), ⟦Matthew 9:16|Mt 9:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:21|27:21⟧, ⟦John 21:10|Jo 21:10⟧, ⟦Acts 5:2|Ac 5:2⟧, al.; also after verbs of eating, etc.;
	⟪(3)⟫ of alienation (cl. gen. of separation), after such verbs as λούω (Deiss., BS, 227), λύω, σώζω, παύω, etc.; ἀνάθεμα ἀ., ⟦Romans 9:3|Ro 9:3⟧; ἀποθνήσκειν ἀ., ⟦Colossians 2:20|Col 2:20⟧; σαλευθῆναι, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:2|II Th 2:2⟧, καθαρός, -ίζειν, ἀ. (Deiss., BS, 196, 216), ⟦Acts 20:26|Ac 20:26⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:1|II Co 7:1⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:14|He 9:14⟧;
	⟪(4)⟫ of position, ⟦Matthew 23:34|Mt 23:34⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:31|24:31⟧, al.; after μακράν, ⟦Matthew 8:30|Mt 8:30⟧; transposed before measures of distance, ⟦John 10:18|Jo 10:18⟧ ⟦John 21:8|21:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 14:20|Re 14:20⟧ (Abbott, JG, 227);
	⟪(5)⟫ of time, ἀπὸ τ. ὥρας, ἡμέρας, etc., ⟦Matthew 9:22|Mt 9:22⟧, ⟦John 19:27|Jo 19:27⟧, ⟦Acts 20:18|Ac 20:18⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:5|Phl 1:5⟧, al.; ἀπ’ αἰῶνος, ⟦Luke 1:70|Lk 1:70⟧, al.; ἀπ’ ἀρχῆς, etc., ⟦Matthew 19:4|Mt 19:4⟧, ⟦Romans 1:20|Ro 1:20⟧; ἀπὸ βρέφους, ⟦2 Timothy 3:15|II Ti 3:15⟧; ἀφ’ ἧς, ⟪since⟫, ⟦Luke 7:45|Lk 7:45⟧, al.; ἀπὸ τ. νῦν, ⟦Luke 1:48|Lk 1:48⟧, al.; ἀπὸ τότε, ⟦Matthew 4:17|Mt 4:17⟧, al.; ἀπὸ πέρυσι, ⟪a year ago⟫, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:10|II Co 8:10⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 9:2|9:2⟧; ἀπὸ πρωΐ, ⟦Acts 28:23|Ac 28:23⟧;
	⟪(6)⟫ of order or rank, ἀπὸ διετοῦς, ⟦Matthew 2:16|Mt 2:16⟧; ἀπὸ Ἀβραάμ, ⟦Matthew 1:17|Mt 1:17⟧; ἕβδομος ἀπὸ Ἀδάμ, ⟦Jude 1:14|Ju 14⟧; ἀπὸ μικροῦ ἕως μεγάλου, ⟦Acts 8:10|Ac 8:10⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:11|He 8:11⟧; ἄρχεσθαι ἀπό, ⟦Matthew 20:8|Mt 20:8⟧, ⟦John 8:9|Jo 8:9⟧, ⟦Acts 8:35|Ac 8:35⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Of origin;
	⟪(1)⟫ of birth, extraction, and hence, in late writers,
		⟪(a)⟫ of local extraction (cl. ἐξ; Abbott, JG, 227 ff.), ⟦Matthew 21:11|Mt 21:11⟧, ⟦Mark 15:43|Mk 15:43⟧, ⟦John 1:45|Jo 1:45⟧, ⟦Acts 10:38|Ac 10:38⟧, al.; οἱ ἀπὸ Ἰταλίας (WM, § 66, 6; M, Pr., 237; Westc, Rendall, in l.), ⟦Hebrews 13:24|He 13:24⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ of membership in a community or society (Bl., § 40, 2), ⟦Acts 12:1|Ac 12:1⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ of material (= cl. gen.; Bl., § 40, 2; M, Pr., 102), ⟦Matthew 3:4|Mt 3:4⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:21|27:21⟧;
		⟪(d)⟫ after verbs of asking, seeking, etc., ⟦Luke 11:50|Lk 11:50⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|51⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:6|I Th 2:6⟧ (Milligan, in l.);
	⟪(2)⟫ of the cause, instrument, means or occasion (freq. = ὑπό, παρά, and after verbs of learning, hearing, knowing, etc.; Bl., § 40, 3), ⟦Matthew 7:16|Mt 7:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 11:29|11:29⟧, ⟦Luke 22:45|Lk 22:45⟧, ⟦Acts 2:22|Ac 2:22⟧ ⟦Acts 4:36|4:36⟧ ⟦Acts 9:13|9:13⟧ ⟦Acts 12:14|12:14⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:23|I Co 11:23⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:2|Ga 3:2⟧, al.; ἀπὸ τ. ὄχλου, ⟦Luke 19:3|Lk 19:3⟧ (cf. ⟦John 21:6|Jo 21:6⟧, ⟦Acts 22:11|Ac 22:11⟧); ἀπὸ τ. φόβου, ⟦Matthew 14:26|Mt 14:26⟧, al. (cf. ⟦Matthew 10:28|Mt 10:28⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:44|13:44⟧).
⟪3.⟫ Noteworthy Hellenistic phrases: φοβεῖσθαι ἀπό (M, Pr., 102, 107); προσέχειν ἀπό (M, Pr., 102, 107; Milligan, NTD, 50); ἀπὸ νότου (Heb. ⁨מִנֶּגֶב⁩), ⟦Revelation 21:13|Re 21:13⟧; ἀπὸ προσώπου (⁨מִפְּנֵי⁩), ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:9|II Th 1:9⟧ (Bl., § 40, 9); ἀπὸ τ. καρδιῶν (⁨בְּלֵב⁩), ⟦Matthew 18:35|Mt 18:35⟧; ἀπὸ ὁ ὤν (WM, § 10, 2; M, Pr., 9), ⟦Revelation 1:4|Re 1:4⟧.
⟪4.⟫ In composition, ἀπό denotes separation, departure, origin, etc. (ἀπολύω, ἀπέρχομαι, ἀπογράφω); it also has a perfective force (M, Pr., 112, 247), as in ἀφικνεῖσθαι, ἀφικνεῖσθαι, q.v.
